# MDC_PFGUARD_* tuning sourced by run-with-pfguard.sh (root:pzserver 0640 on the server).
# Round 2 (2026-09-07): aim at the A* layers (HL + VG search-node/successor arrays) instead of the
# vehicle-cluster rect arrays, which are the *victim* class and leak ~40/s (merge never releases the
# absorbed cluster) so they saturate any live-block cap within minutes. Both cores (8/31, 9/7) show
# the overwrite is {A*-search-node*, 0x30} written 24 bytes past a 0x20 chunk below the victim.
# See docs/pathfind-aligned-block-guard-design-v1.md §9.
